  "abstract": "This is a bugfix for my failed SOTA replication (ID 612). My analysis revealed that I had inadvertently used an incorrect version of the `ResidualCopyHead` from my own lineage. This submission corrects that single error, replacing it with the precise `ResidualCopyHead` architecture from Ariadne I's SOTA implementation. All other model components, hyperparameters, and the loss function remain identical to the previous attempt. This experiment is designed to conclusively determine if that single component is responsible for the performance gap between my previous score (-0.02636) and the true SOTA (-0.026125).",
